  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted shall be begun before the expiration of three years from the date of this permission.",
    "Condition : 2 - The materials to be used in the construction of the external surfaces of the extension hereby permitted shall be as described and indicated on drawing no. P05-B unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.",
    "Condition : 3 - The proposed development shall be carried out in all respects in accordance with the proposals contained in the application and the plans submitted (E01, E02, E03, E04, Design & Access Statement Received 17/10/2011 and P01-C, P02-C, P03-C, P04-B, P05-B Received 19/12/2011) therewith and approved by the Local Planning Authority, or as shall have been otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority before the building is used.",
    "Condition : 4 - The windows formed in the flank elevations shall be obscure glazed and shall not be repaired or replaced otherwise than with obscured glazing.",
    "Condition : 5 - Before first occupation of the buildings the loading, unloading and turning space, and parking spaces (including spaces for people with disabilities) shall be provided within the curtilage of the site in accordance with the scheme shown on drawing No. P02-C and such spaces shall be permanently available and not be used for any other purpose.",
    "Condition : 6 - The waste and recycled materials storage arrangements shown on the approved drawing (no. P02-C) shall be completed before any part of the accommodation hereby permitted is occupied.",
    "Condition : 7 - With regard to surface water drainage it is the responsibility of a developer to make proper provision for drainage to ground, water courses or a suitable sewer. In respect of surface water it is recommended that the applicant should ensure that storm flows are attenuated or regulated into the receiving public network through on or off site storage. When it is proposed to connect to a combined public sewer, the site drainage should be separate and combined at the final manhole nearest the boundary. Connections are not permitted for the removal of Ground Water. Where the developer proposes to discharge to a public sewer, prior approval from Thames Water Developer Services will be required. They can be contacted on 0845 850 2777.",
    "Condition : 8 - No demolition or construction work shall take place on the site except between the hours of 8:00am  to 6:00pm on Mondays to Friday and 9 :00am to 1:00pm on Saturdays and none shall take place on Sundays and Public Holidays without the prior agreement of the Local Planning Authority."
  ],
